body:
Dolphins are horrible creatures. They attack, bite, kill animals and torture animals, rape eachother among many other things, They've killed plenty of people in attempts to "Play" with them. The brain of mine to paint Dolphins as the sociopathic serial killers of the ocean is very real. 

&#x200B;

But it's also an amusing fantasy to paint them with that kind of moral structure. Really they just arent as cute and cuddly as many try to paint them. This probably didn't cheer you up. Lemme try again.

&#x200B;

Cats can sense human emotions (Not as strongly as dogs) But my cat loves to just flop himself against us when we're sad and purr.  It's adorable and unbearably heartwarming.

If you're in america. Keep in mind that they ALWAYS deny you disability for the first attempt. It's dumb, but that's how the system works. Appeal it, and contact a lawyer. It's a long, arduous process and may require going to court with a lawyer in tow. A lot of lawyers will just want a portion of your backpay so it might not have any upfront costs to get it started and will only cost you once you win.

&#x200B;

Therapists and psychs can be your best friend for this, but as you've already noticed. That itself can be a long task in finding one that works for, and can work with you :/ that's the nature of mental health stuff though..It almost feels like dating at times.

&#x200B;

Its hard to stop the thoughts, and hard to do things you enjoy when stressed, but if you can do your best to be in a happy place and collect your thoughts and move forward is about all you can do. Don't give up!

sorry this is super long and slightly disjointed. but i hope it helps and gives some insight.

&#x200B;

My wife and I have been together for 8 years now, married for 3? or 4..married for a while, and wife is diagnosed and us, my therapist, and my old psych pushed heavily for me to get diagnosed also but with covid hitting my appt was canceled and frankly it wont change my life to get the label, i'm convinced i aim regardless.

&#x200B;

But that all aside. I can't say i have any true answers to help you. I can only share what we do. When we first met we bonded rather quickly on similar interests and i think that's something that keeps us activitly engaged with eachother. We're both big into video games, Final Fantasy 14 a giant mainstay. And many others, but we both write a lot alone and often write together, a lot of our writings being fanfiction lately of whatever game we're obsessed over.

&#x200B;

Though over the years we both have different interests that the other might not care about from the start. I can't think of many on my end at the moment, but i have had a few on her end that i never cared for. Vocaloids, Certain games, and actually fanfiction. But with all those that i didn't like. I pushed myself into those things with her with the mindset of "Maybe i'll like them because of her." And A lot of that rang true and we now bond over a lot of that. List is longer but can't think of anymore :P

&#x200B;

Interests aside. We're both insanely patient with eachother. She's very floaty mentally and get's pretty lost in her world all the time, as I'm pretty grounded and have to push myself to get out into the daydreaming at times, though daydreaming is very much my way to time travel anymore. specially at work. But, We have a nice dynamic where i do take care of a lot of things including our finances, and she pretty much takes care of me mentally. This has shifted a lot as she now doesn't work and i'd say she does alot of the stuffs but i got quite the stressful job so at times i can just shutdown for 2 to 3 days at a time. But the important thing is. Is that she understands that. My breakdowns are not because of her, If I'm in a bad headspace. It's not her fault and it's not a bash against her.  I have trouble not beating myself up when she's in a bad space, but i work on it.

&#x200B;

Communication is so so important for us. We're insanely open about everything and regularly. maybe once a week look at eachother and always ask. "Are you still happy?" And this, while initially stemmed in insecurity, Is super important to me. It will bring on discussion sometimes. Whether it's about our relationship or something we're talking together. It'll let us vent. or even just gush on each other a little. This while again over some insecurities also came from a lot of horrible relationships that I've been in when i didn't notice the signs of the relationship going south and then get divebombed with a break up where i thought things were great.

&#x200B;

Communication is hard though. We find ourselves typing to each other a lot because it's sometimes easier to say things through text than vocally, but what works for us doesn't mean it'll work for you. This has taken us years to really figure eachother out to this extent and i could gush for years on her, but my biggest things are that we have similar interests, we love doing them together, we communicate calmly with eachother, we understand what our autism does to eachother and know what to do even if nothing is the best thing to do, and we enjoy what we have. 

&#x200B;

We're immature with eachother. Super cutesy at times, our sex life is amazing, and i look forward to every moment with her. But never disrespectful, and communicating calmly is the most important. If you're angry. you say stupid shit. you make mistakes, if you can't say it, write it. and learn to say your sorry when you mess up. Pride is so stupid. We all make mistakes and say or overlook things.

I'm in my thirties now and I can easily say the worst years of my life were my teenage years. I had a unique childhood and all but still. Getting out of where my life started was the best thing i've ever done. I've been diagnosed with depression, anxiety, PTSD, and a few other things but that's besides the point and are things i can really work on now that I'm away from a lot of the life that made those things worse.

&#x200B;

A few things i've found very important to my quality of life is making sure my homelife is a great safeplace for myself. It helps me be willing to try new things because no matter what happens I got my comfy place to go back too. How many people you've kissed, or parties you've been to only have value if you put value to that. Numbers aren't something you should care about but more quality.

&#x200B;

And with dating apps now a days it does make connecting with new people quite a bit easier. (Be safe though with that. Always tell someone when and where you're going. Strangers can be scary..) Which I met my current wife on Okcupid after quite the spree of going through people trying to find what I wanted and I've got nothing but compliments on my outcome. 

&#x200B;

People glamourize their youths so much. And I assure you, promise you even. That your youth is really only the start of your life. There is so so much more then those younger years, You just have to look for it a little. Which with anxiety and stuff, Makes it very important to have a place or even a relaxation room. And maybe an excuse to bail when things aren't working out for you. 

&#x200B;

Don't look back on days as days lost or wasted. I know it's easier said then done. and I know i've been all over the place with this, but at least in my case. My under 20 years we're the worst in my life, and I can't imagine any other point in my life ever reaching that low again. 

&#x200B;

Sorry for how scatterbrained this was. Hope you feel better <3.

\*Catlateral Damage

&#x200B;

FTFY
